## Q3 — Terms of Use vs DPA — what's praxis 🟢
- **Self-serve SaaS:** customer click-accepts **Terms of Use (Product)** + Privacy + Cookie. Terms of Use *is* the contract.
- **Enterprise/negotiated** (Marketplace, hosting): a **negotiated Main Agreement** (or Marketplace Order + Microsoft Standard Contract) is the contract, with its own commercial terms (your **Attachment 1 – Terms of Service**). The click-through Terms of Use does **not** apply — the negotiated agreement replaces it.
- **The DPA does NOT fill the Terms role.** It's a separate **data-protection** layer (GDPR Art. 28) that sits *under* whichever contract applies. Terms/Main Agreement = the commercial+service deal; DPA = how personal data is processed.

→ So Terms of Use is the self-serve contract; enterprise uses the Main Agreement (+ Attachment 1); the DPA is an annex in both, never a substitute for Terms.

**Applicability matrix:**

| Document | Self-serve SaaS | Enterprise – Marketplace | Enterprise – Hosting |
|---|---|---|---|
| *Governing commercial contract* | Terms of Use (Product) — click-accept | Order + Microsoft Standard Contract | Main Agreement + Attachment 1 (Terms of Service) |
| **Terms of Use (Product)** | ✅ it *is* the contract | ❌ MS Standard Contract governs | ❌ Main Agreement governs |
| **Privacy Policy (Product)** | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| **Cookie Policy** | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| **DPA** | ⚠️ none today — gap (click-through DPA?) | ✅ Marketplace DPA (14-day notice) | ✅ Attachment 3 hosting DPA (30-day notice) |
| *SLA (Attachment 2)* | ⚠️ none / best-effort? (confirm) | ✅ via publisher SLA / Attachment 2 (99%) | ✅ Attachment 2 (99%) |

Notes: Privacy Policy – Website + Cookie Policy also apply to the marketing funnel for everyone (not motion-specific). ⚠️ = assumption to confirm.

